# Release notes for v2.5.3

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v2.5.3.oot

Logline: One-tree std climb: nested domain tail, domain-root invariants, canary eviction, and qa keepers.

Setup: ooda.pkg version=2.5.3. Tag v2.5.3. Proof: emit-c + gcc + run on a keeper import.

Beats:
  1. Nested 197 std top-level dirs into 33 domain parents. Trunk stayed. Tail under hw compile phys chem bio robot econ data ai ui.
  2. File role is not a folder. Laws live in their domain. principles/ is cross-domain bounds only (CODATA k_B, Landauer).
  3. One DomainCert type in std/core/domain_cert.oo. Each remaining root has <domain>_invariants.oo. Algebraic identity is computed, not a name stub.
  4. Deleted 6383 unused canaries (prove_prod_* mass plus unused prove/proof_verifiers). Moved 15 live keepers to qa/formal_proofs, qa/prove, qa/proof_verifiers. Rewrote 29 imports. canaries/ is gone.
  5. Import strings follow the nested paths. Path freeze: Delta_path = 0. No new std/ top-level dirs.

What this proves:
  * A library is an imported module. A prove file is not a library.
  * stage50_release_lock_smoke loads qa/prove/master_release_verifier.oo and prints PASSED.
  * std/README.oot maps 33 parents. Named product proves stay in fixtures/prove_prod_*.oo.

Out of scope: generate_shipped.oo was not re-run. Duplicate Galois/BLAS merge is still residual. oodac Result-helper C redefinition on SAT import is a compiler residual, not a path miss.
